<% title "Family plan" %>
<%= render "users/nav", selected: :settings_billing %>

<h1 class="heading"><span class="flex-grow">Family plan</span></h1>

<% if params[:subscribed].present? %>
  <%= render "application/callout", type: "success", title: "Welcome to the family plan" do %>
    <p class="mb-0">Once Stripe confirms the payment (usually seconds), your family can run
      more than one venture and use API keys. The take-rate stays
      <%= number_to_percentage(Event::Plan::Pro::REVENUE_FEE * 100, precision: 1) %> —
      the same as Free. Pro does not discount the fee.</p>
  <% end %>
<% end %>

<div class="card mt2">
  <% if @subscription&.active? %>
    <h3 class="mt0">You're on the family plan 🎉</h3>
    <p>
      Unlimited ventures and API keys, one subscription.
      <%# FUIME 2026-09-14: this plan is retired and buys nothing. Said at the
          top, in the parent's terms, because the alternative is a family
          quietly paying $19.99 a month for a feature set every account now
          has. Fuime should not need to be asked for that money back. %>
      <strong>This subscription no longer gives you anything.</strong>
      Fuime moved to one flat price — <strong><%= Event::Plan.fuime_price_label %></strong>
      of what each business collects, no monthly fee — and unlimited businesses
      and API keys are now included for everyone. Please cancel it below; you
      will not lose anything.
      <% if @subscription.current_period_end %>
        Renews <%= @subscription.current_period_end.strftime("%B %-d, %Y") %><%= @subscription.cancel_at_period_end ? " (set to cancel)" : "" %>.
      <% end %>
    </p>
    <%# Fuime: a comped plan has no Stripe customer behind it, so the portal would
        have nothing to open. Say who gave it to them instead of showing a button
        that answers "nothing to manage yet". %>
    <% if @subscription.comped? %>
      <p class="muted mb-0">Fuime comped this plan for your family, so there's nothing to pay and no card on file.</p>
    <% elsif @is_adult %>
      <%# Fuime: turbo: false is load-bearing — see the Upgrade button below. %>
      <%= button_to "Cancel this subscription", my_billing_portal_path, class: "btn", form: { data: { turbo: false } } %>
      <p class="muted text-sm mt-1">Cancellation and invoices happen in Stripe's secure portal — Fuime never sees your card.</p>
    <% end %>
  <% elsif @subscription&.stripe_backed? %>
    <%# past_due / unpaid / incomplete still have a live Stripe subscription.
        Upgrade would open a second Checkout session; the portal is the writer. %>
    <h3 class="mt0">There's already a subscription on this account</h3>
    <p>
      Stripe has this family as <strong><%= @subscription.status.humanize.downcase %></strong>.
      Update the card or pay the invoice from the billing portal. Starting another
      subscription would charge you twice.
    </p>
    <% if @is_adult %>
      <%= button_to "Manage billing", my_billing_portal_path, class: "btn btn--secondary", form: { data: { turbo: false } } %>
      <p class="muted text-sm mt-1 mb-0">Card changes and invoices happen in Stripe's secure portal — Fuime never sees your card.</p>
    <% end %>
  <% elsif @just_paid %>
    <%# Fuime: back from Stripe Checkout, before the webhook has landed.
        `@subscription` is written by `customer.subscription.created`, which
        arrives a beat after Stripe redirects the payer back here. In that gap
        the page fell through to the Free-plan branch and rendered the green
        "Welcome to the family plan" callout directly above a live
        "Upgrade — $19.99/mo" button. A parent who pressed it — and the callout
        is exactly what invites a second press, since nothing else on the page
        says the plan is on — opened a second Checkout and was charged twice.
        Every other double-subscription path was already guarded
        (Fuime::BillingController#subscribe sends an existing stripe_backed
        record to the portal); this was the one window where no record exists yet.
        No Upgrade button here. On any later visit, without ?subscribed=1, the
        page reads the real record again — so a webhook that genuinely never
        arrives still leaves a way to buy. %>
    <h3 class="mt0">Confirming your payment</h3>
    <p class="mb-0">
      Stripe has your payment and we're waiting for it to confirm — usually a few
      seconds. Refresh this page in a moment. Don't pay again: starting another
      subscription would charge you twice.
    </p>
  <% else %>
    <%# FUIME 2026-09-14: there is no upgrade, because there is no second tier.
        The whole branch that lived here — a Free-vs-family comparison, an
        Upgrade button, and three different ways of telling a teenager to go ask
        an adult for one — went away with the family plan. What is left is the
        price, stated once.

        Note this screen is now the same for a teen and a parent. The old
        @is_adult / @pending_guardian_invite / @guardians branching existed only
        to decide who was allowed to enter a card, and nobody enters a card any
        more. %>
    <h3 class="mt0">Your plan</h3>
    <p>
      One price: Fuime keeps
      <strong><%= Event::Plan.fuime_price_label %></strong>
      of what your business collects, and nothing at all until you sell
      something. No monthly fee.
    </p>
    <p class="mb-0">
      <strong>Unlimited businesses</strong> and <strong>API keys</strong> are
      included. Selling at a scale where this stops making sense?
      <a href="mailto:support@fuime.com">Talk to us</a> about custom pricing.
    </p>
  <% end %>
</div>

<p class="muted text-sm mt-3 mb-0">
  Fuime is a financial technology company, not a bank. The subscription covers Fuime's software;
  payment processing on venture sales is provided by Stripe and itemised separately.
</p>
